  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 350°F and line two baking sheets with parchment paper.",
    "Cream the butter, granulated sugar and brown sugar with a mixer until fluffy, 2-3 minutes.",
    "Add the eggs and vanilla and beat until light in color and creamy.",
    "Add the flour, black cocoa, crushed Oreos, baking soda, baking powder and salt. Mix on low until completely combined with no dry streaks.",
    "Portion the dough into 1/2 cup balls (about 12). Place 6 on each sheet and press each down into a thick hockey puck about 1 inch tall.",
    "Bake 12-15 minutes, until the tops are no longer glossy. Cool on the pan 20 minutes.",
    "While the cookies cool, make the frosting: beat the butter, cream cheese and vanilla until smooth, then beat in the powdered sugar 1 cup at a time. Add milk 1 tsp at a time only if it is too stiff to pipe.",
    "Spoon the frosting into a gallon zip-top bag, snip one corner, and pipe a spiral onto each still-warm cookie. Sprinkle with crushed Oreos.",
    "Serve warm or at room temperature. Store leftovers airtight in the refrigerator."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Black cocoa is what gives the Oreo color and flavor; regular or Dutch-process cocoa makes a lighter brown cookie."
  ],
